One common way improper API usage leads to vulnerabilities is through **Path Traversal**. This occurs when an application uses user-supplied input to construct a file path without properly validating or sanitizing the input, allowing an attacker to access sensitive files on the server (like `/etc/passwd`).

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.*;

public class FileServer {
    public void readFile(String filename) throws IOException {
        // VULNERABLE: This code directly concatenates user input to a base directory.
        // An attacker could pass "../../etc/passwd" to escape the intended directory.
        File baseDir = new File("/var/www/uploads/");
        File fileToRead = new File(baseDir, filename);

        byte[] content = Files.readAllBytes(fileToRead.toPath());
        System.out.println(new String(content));
    }
}
```

